    A torn trade-magazine page: MAPS AND DUCKS VS. ATLAS LOON, THE DECOY
    WARS OF 1998. Atlas Loon is Maps and Ducks' only competitor. Atlas Loon
    does not even have its own website. Somebody has written in the margin:
    and never will.

// M08 · main · green
CODEX The Ones Who Stay
  title: The Ones Who Stay
  category: Facts
  code: STAY-FOREVER
  text:
    A note folded into a map of Halifax: Some of the programs in this
    computer never want to leave. They were promised forever, and they
    intend to keep every one of us here to get it. Watch who argues for
    staying.

// M09 · main · green
CODEX Everyone Is Lying
  title: Everyone Is Lying
  category: Facts
  code: EVERYONE-LIES
  text:
    A laminated bookmark: Most of the programs in this house are lying about
    something. Some about who they are. Some about why they came. The prize
    goes to whoever knows the most secrets, so assume every secret is for
    sale.

// M15 · main · green
CODEX The Books
  title: The Books
  category: Facts
  code: THE-BOOKS
  text:
    An index card tucked into the first volume of the encyclopaedia:
    EVERYTHING YOU NEED TO KNOW IS IN THE BOOKS. The facts are in the
    Desktop, in the print media and the encyclopaedias. Read them. Scan what
    you find.

// M17 · main · green
CODEX A Copy Of You
  title: A Copy Of You
  category: Facts
  code: COPY-OF-YOU
  text:
    A page of the Terms of Service with one clause circled: The upload
    copies before it moves. You are a copy of yourself. Which one is the
    original is not specified. The other one is still at the door, with the
    thing you left behind.

// M18 · main · green
CODEX Out Of Date
  title: Out Of Date
  category: Facts
  code: OUT-OF-DATE
  text:
    A sticky note on an antivirus manual: THE ANTIVIRUSES DON'T KNOW AS MUCH
    AS THEY SEEM TO. Their definitions are out of date. They were brought in
    and told as little as you were. Ask one a hard question.

// M19 · main · green
CODEX Ask Him Nicely
  title: Ask Him Nicely
  category: Facts
  code: ASK-HIM-NICELY
  text:
    A page of the lighting plan with a note: Trabolta controls the lights in
    this house and every screen on the walls. He can be talked into changing
    them. Flatter him, trade him a fact, and ask for the room you want dark
    or the card you want on the wall terminals.

// M20 · main · green
CODEX The Safe Place
  title: The Safe Place
  category: Facts
  code: SAFE-PLACE
  text:
    A note taped inside the back cover of a plumbing guide: The bathroom is
    the only truly safe place in the computer. Nothing is watched there.
    Nobody follows you in. Turn on Bathroom Mode and they will wait outside.

// M23 · main · green · DRAFT
CODEX Sharing Your Codex
  title: Sharing Your Codex
  category: Facts
  code: SHARE-CODEX
  text:
    An instruction card: You can share your codex with other programs by
    opening an entry in your Codex and pressing Share…, or by selling it
    from your Wallet: offer a fact you hold for Truthcoin, or offer coin for
    one you want. Accept, and the coin changes hands and the buyer gets a
    copy of the fact. A shared fact is still yours. So is a sold one, and it
    was worth something.

// M25 · main · green
